course: dictionary
lesson: 1353
title: Candid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Candid means honest and open. A candid person says what they really think, even when it is hard to hear. «Her candid answer was that the cake was burnt.» She did not hide the truth, so candid tells you she was honest.
explain: Use the context to check. «Less than candid» is an official way to say dishonest. If less than candid means dishonest, then candid is the opposite: open and honest. Try swapping in honest: «less than honest» also means dishonest, so the meaning fits.
explain: Candid has a second meaning for photos. A candid photo is taken when people do not know they are being photographed, so they look natural and not posed. «The candid shot caught Grandma laughing at her own joke.» Nobody was posing for that picture.
fact: Candid means honest and open, saying what you really think.
fact: «A candid answer» is a truthful answer, even if it is hard to hear.
fact: «A candid photo» is taken without people knowing or posing.
fact: «To be candid» means to be honest.
fact: «Candid about» means open and honest about something, as in «He was candid about his mistakes.»
exercise: «Her candid answer surprised everyone.» What does candid mean here? | Quiet and shy | Tired and bored | Angry and loud | *Honest and open
exercise: «The candid photo showed Dad laughing, not posing.» What is a candid photo? | A very blurry picture of the sky | A photo with a fancy frame | *A photo taken without people posing or knowing
exercise: Which phrase means the same as «to be honest»? | To be loud | To be lost | *To be candid | To be quick
test: «Less than candid» is a polite way to say what? | *Dishonest | Lost in the rain | Very happy | Very tired
test: «He was candid about his mistakes.» What does this tell you about him? | *He was open and honest about them | He forgot them all | He was angry with his friends | He hid them from everyone
exam: Kira says «candid» means shy, but her teacher says it means honest and open. Which is right, and how can you check? | Both are right, so it does not matter | Neither, because candid means loud | Kira is right, because candid means shy | *The teacher is right, and you can check by swapping honest into «a candid answer» and seeing if it still makes sense
